From: fpvOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] drm/artosyn: scale any I420 picture to the screen, up or down

The video plane scaled only 1920x1080 onto a 1280x720 screen, so 720p and
864p video on a 1080p screen (and 864p on 720p) was refused and the
receiver dropped every frame. The scaler takes a ratio per axis and the
three-tap filter's 17 phases interpolate at any ratio: accept I420 up to
2x smaller or larger on each axis and load the filter at every output
size (it was loaded only at 720p).

A new source size is not a modeset (that dropped HDMI and the screen went
black while it resynced): its scaler registers must not change while a
frame scans out, so that one flip is written from the next frame-start
interrupt. Its event is kept with it, not armed on the vblank queue, and
sent one interrupt later: it cannot go out before the flip is written,
the old buffer is not handed back while it may still be scanned, and no
other commit starts in between. A format change stays a modeset. The
scaler is on when either axis differs from the screen, as the check
accepts.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/artosyn_vo.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/artosyn/artosyn_vo.c
@@ -107,6 +107,16 @@
